  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LLF - Abidjan &amp; 11 Secondary Cities Sanitation Project in Cote d&apos;Ivoire</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to help achieving a sustainable improvement in the provision of sanitation services in Abidjan and 11 secondary cities by: (i) eliminating uncontrolled dumping of sludge, thus protecting the populations and the environment against water borne diseases, sewage flooding and discharge of untreated effluents; (ii) preventing ground and surface water pollution as well as; (iii) supporting the possible value added use of the treated fecal sludge and other substances in an environmental and economic sustainable way (use of methane gas to generate electricity and dry sludge as fertilizer in agriculture, etc). The project will significantly improve living conditions by reducing environmental pollution in the targeted cities, while improving health and sanitary conditions of the population.</narrative>
  </description>
